## 5. FILE-BY-FILE BREAKDOWN

### 5.1 `backend/server.js`

**Purpose:** Main backend — all HTTP routes, scheduled tasks, DB operations.

**Structure (section-wise):**

| Section | Content |
|---|---|
| §1 Imports | Express, bcrypt, JWT, pg, crypto, Angel_REST, Angel_WS |
| §2 Config | DB pool, JWT secret, load STOCKS from JSON, STRATEGIES config, passesStrategy() |
| §3 Time / Phases | `getIST()`, `getScreenerPhase()` (closed/forming/ready/weekend), holiday checks |
| §4 ORB State | In-memory Map + `loadOrbStateFromDB()`, `getOrbState()` |
| §5 WebSocket | `handleTick()` (3-stage logic), `startWebSocketForReadyPhase()`, watchdog timer |
| §6 Middleware | `auth`, `adminOnly`, `log`, `generateUsername`, `generatePassword`, TOTP verify |
| §7 Auth | `/api/login`, `/api/complete-login`, `/api/session-check`, `/api/logout` |
| §8 Forgot | `/api/forgot-password/check`, `/api/forgot-password/reset` |
| §9 Password | `/api/change-password`, `/api/me` (profile) |
| §10 Users CRUD | GET/POST/PUT/DELETE users + renew, set-expiry, reset, disable |
| §11 Audit + Prices | `/api/audit`, `/api/prices` |
| §12 Holidays | `/api/admin/holidays` GET/POST/DELETE |
| §13 Screener | `/api/stocks`, `/api/screener/status`, `/api/screener/data`, `/api/screener/fetch-batch`, `/api/screener/ltp` |
| §14 Closing | `fetchClosingPrices()` (15:34 IST scheduler), `/api/admin/force-ltp` |
| §15 DB Loader | `loadScreenerCacheFromDB()` (rehydrate memory on boot) |
| §16 Start | `app.listen()` + boot sequence |

**Critical flows:**

1. **Server boot:**
   - Load holidays from DB
   - Login to Angel One
   - Load 9:15 candles from DB into memory cache
   - Load ORB states from DB
   - Schedule closing fetch at 15:34 IST
   - Start WS watchdog (checks every 60s)

2. **Phase detection (`getScreenerPhase`):**
   - Weekend/holiday → `weekend`, date = previous trading day
   - Before 9:15 IST → `closed`
   - 9:15–9:30 IST → `forming`
   - After 9:30 IST → `ready`, date = today

3. **WebSocket watchdog:**
   - Every 60s: if phase is `ready`, call `startWebSocketForReadyPhase()`
   - If phase not `ready` and WS running, stop WS

**Exports:** None (entry point).

