### 5.2 `backend/brokers/angelone/Angel_REST.js`

**Purpose:** All Angel One REST API logic. No business logic here.

**Key exports:**

| Function | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `loginPlatform()` | Auto-login with TOTP from env |
| `getSessionStatus()` | Returns `{ loggedIn, expiresAt, loginTime }` |
| `getCandlesForToken(token, date)` | Fetch + aggregate 9:15–9:30 candle |
| `getCandlesForTokens(tokens, date)` | Batch fetch (5 workers, 150 req/min cap) |
| `getCachedCandles(tokens, date)` | Read from memory (no API) |
| `setCachedCandle(token, date, candle)` | Write to memory (used by server for DB rehydration) |
| `setCachedLTP(token, price)` | Cache an LTP value |
| `getCachedLTP(token)` | Read cached LTP |
| `getLTPForTokens(tokens)` | Batch LTP fetch (50/call, market hours only) |
| `getClosingPriceForToken(token, date)` | Fetch 15:30 close via 1-min candle |
| `fetchAllClosingPrices(tokens, date)` | Bulk closing fetch (batched) |
| `fetchAllLTP(tokens)` | Bulk LTP fetch |
| `getFeedToken()` | Returns WebSocket feed token from session |
| `getFailedList(date)` | Failed candle list |
| `clearCandleCache()`, `clearLtpCache()` | Reset memory |

**Rate limiting:**
- Global token bucket: 150 req/min (configurable via `ANGEL_CANDLE_RATE_PER_MIN`)
- 5 parallel workers
- 8s cooldown on HTTP 403/429
- Circuit breaker: 10 consecutive failures → abort batch
- Text-first parsing (no blind `r.json()`)

**Cache structure:**
- `candleCache: Map<"token_date", [ts, open, high, low, close, volume]>`
- `ltpCache: Map<token, { price, ts }>` — 30s TTL
- `session: { jwtToken, feedToken, expiresAt, loginTime }`

**Angel One API endpoints used:**
- Login: `/rest/auth/angelbroking/user/v1/loginByPassword`
- Candles: `/rest/secure/angelbroking/historical/v1/getCandleData`
- LTP: `/rest/secure/angelbroking/market/v1/quote`

**Interval format:** `ONE_MINUTE` (aggregated 15 bars for 9:15–9:30 range).

